        "detail": "• Oct 15: Dennis published two public PETadex corpora on Hugging Face: petadex-corpus-full (307,155,746 ORFs: PAZy 211, NR 4,723,128, Logan 302,432,407; 41.6 GB, 22 configs) and petadex-corpus-centroids90 (18,172,960 rows, one per 90% identity cluster).\n• Oct 15: An exact-MD5 join found only 401 of 1,219 labelled sequences in the published corpus, with just 21 appearing anywhere in the 302M-ORF Logan population, so the recommendation was to train on sequence alone and treat corpus columns as diagnostics.\n• Oct 15: Dennis published the two PETadex HuggingFace repos: petadex-corpus-full (155 files, 41.6 GB, 22 Parquet configs) and petadex-corpus-centroids90 (3.9 GB, 57 columns), both public and ungated with license pending while PAZy, AlphaFold DB and NCBI redistribution terms are reviewed.\n• Oct 15: The PlasticESM LoRA adapter was confirmed trained on the 18.2M 90% centroids rather than all 307M ORFs, settling an earlier 18M versus 300M ambiguity, but the published checkpoint kept only 1.84M of 14.75M trained adapter parameters and recovery is closed.\n• Oct 16: The 60% identity centroid ESMFold2 fold finished: 1,793,781 structures over 851.6 GPU-hours, with every input sequence having a verified structure and none failing to fold. 123,940 Full (under 150 aa) and 1,667,455 Fast (150 to 1,740 aa) finished on L40S about 14.5 hours after launch, and the 2,386 long Fast folds finished on H100 at 15:36."
